+
+`STEP_BEAD_ID` is closed in step 10, before the drain. That close is the
+whole reason this step can be trusted to run once: the molecule carries
+`gc.session_affinity=require`, so a step bead left open keeps the pool
+respawning the same named session, whose `gc hook --claim --json` hands it this
+already-completed step with no context that the work is done (gcp-rz8a). Never
+substitute `$GC_BEAD_ID` here — for a polecat that is the convoy the molecule
+was poured on, not this step, and closing it would close work that is still
+live.
+
+**2. Already-submitted guard (idempotent re-entry).**
+
+A re-entered submit-and-exit must not re-write bead state. Step 8 sets the
+assignee and clears `gc.routed_to`; run a second time on a bead the refinery
+has since parked, it silently pulls that bead back out of an escalation. Bail
+out before touching anything when all three marks of a completed handoff are
+present — target recorded, branch on origin at this commit, and the bead handed
+to somebody who is not this session:
+
+```bash
+SUBMITTED_JSON=$(gc bd show "$WORK_BEAD_ID" --json)
+SUBMITTED_TARGET=$(printf '%s' "$SUBMITTED_JSON" | jq -r '.[0].metadata.target // empty')
+SUBMITTED_BRANCH=$(printf '%s' "$SUBMITTED_JSON" | jq -r '.[0].metadata.branch // empty')
+SUBMITTED_ASSIGNEE=$(printf '%s' "$SUBMITTED_JSON" | jq -r '.[0].assignee // empty')
+SUBMITTED_REMOTE=""
+if [ -n "$SUBMITTED_BRANCH" ]; then
+    SUBMITTED_REMOTE=$(git ls-remote origin "refs/heads/$SUBMITTED_BRANCH" 2>/dev/null | awk '{print $1}')
+fi
+if [ -n "$SUBMITTED_TARGET" ] && [ -n "$SUBMITTED_REMOTE" ] &&
+   [ "$SUBMITTED_REMOTE" = "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" ] &&
+   [ -n "$SUBMITTED_ASSIGNEE" ] && [ "$SUBMITTED_ASSIGNEE" != "$STEP_SESSION" ]; then
+    echo "ALREADY_SUBMITTED $WORK_BEAD_ID target=$SUBMITTED_TARGET branch=$SUBMITTED_BRANCH assignee=$SUBMITTED_ASSIGNEE"
+    echo "Handoff already completed. Closing this step bead and draining without re-writing bead state."
+    [ -n "$STEP_BEAD_ID" ] && gc bd close "$STEP_BEAD_ID" --reason "submit-and-exit: already submitted; no bead state re-written"
+    gc runtime drain-ack
+    exit 0
+fi
+```
+
+All three marks are required together on purpose. `metadata.target` alone
+proves nothing — a caller may set it before dispatch to choose the base branch
+— and an unassigned bead with the branch on origin is the shape a witness
+salvage push leaves behind (gcp-7bo9), which is not a handoff this step
+performed.
+
